    <name>
      <text>Infant Mortality and its Measures_q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given below is the data relating to infant deaths and births in Guatemala, taking the unit of measurement as \('000'\) for live births and deaths .</p>
<br>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th>1959</th>
    <th>1960</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>{@d2@} (Late neonatal deaths in \(1959\))</td>
    <td>{@d4@} (Late neonatal deaths in \(1960\))</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>{@d1@} (Early neonatal deaths in \(1959\))</td>
    <td>{@d3@} (Early neonatal deaths in \(1960\))</td>
  </tr>
 
</table>
</p>
<p></p>
<p>Given the total number of live births in Guatemala in the year \(1959\) and \(1960\) as {@b1@} and {@b2@} respectfully, answer the questions below.</p>
<br>
<p>Note: Leave your answer to correct \(2\) dp</p>
<p></p>
<p>a) Calculate crude infant mortality rate \(=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>b) Determine Infant mortality rate by product formula \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th>1959</th>
    <th>1960</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>\({@d2@} \,\, D_{2}\) (Late neonatal deaths in \(1959\) )</td>
    <td>\({@d4@} \,D_{4}\) (Late neonatal deaths in \(1960\) )</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>\({@d1@} \,D_{1}\) (Early neonatal deaths in \(1959\))</td>
    <td>\({@d3@} \,D_{3}\) (Early neonatal deaths in \(1960\))</td>
  </tr>
 
</table>
</p>
<p>a). Crude infant mortality rate </p>
<p>To find Crude infant mortality rate, we use the formula \(\displaystyle\left [ \frac{D_1+D_2}{B_1}  \right ] \times 1000\) </p>
<p>Applying the formula </p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle\left [ \frac{D_1+D_2}{B_1}  \right ] \times 1000&=\displaystyle \frac{{@d1@}+{@d2@}}{{@b1@}} \times 1000\\
&=\displaystyle \frac{{@d1+d2@}}{{@b1@}} \times 1000\\
&={@ta1@}
\end{align}\)
</p>
<br>
<p>b). Determining Infant mortality rate by product formula</p>
<p>Infant mortality rate by product formula is given the formula below</p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle \left [ 1-\left [ \displaystyle \frac{B_2-D_4}{B_2} \right ] \left [ \displaystyle \frac{B_1-D_2-D_3}{B_1-D_2} \right ]  \right ] \times 1000&=\displaystyle \left [ 1-\left [ \displaystyle \frac{{@b2@}-{@d4@}}{{@b2@}} \right ] \left [ \displaystyle \frac{{@b1@}-{@d2@}-{@d3@}}{{@b1@}-{@d2@}} \right ]  \right ] \times 1000\\
&=\displaystyle \left [ 1-\left [ \displaystyle \frac{{@b2-d4@}}{{@b2@}} \right ] \left [ \displaystyle \frac{{@b1-d2-d3@}}{{@b1-d2@}} \right ]  \right ] \times 1000\\
&={@ta2@}\\
\end{align}\)
</p>]]></text>
